<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20119" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Haemŏnĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aemŏnia</span></b> ),
		ae, f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a poetical name of Thessaly</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 1,
				568</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 543</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 815</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">id. R. Am. 249</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. F. 5,
				381</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nivalis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 37, 20</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Haemŏnĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Hœmonia</i> (<i>Thessaly</i>), <i>Hœmonian</i> (<i>Thessalian</i>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 1, 10, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbs,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Trachin</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					M. 11, 652</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Acastus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 11, 410</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">juvenis,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Jason</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 7, 132</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puer,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Achilles</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. F.
					5, 400</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equi,</span>”
				i. e. <i>of Achilles</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Tr. 3, 11, 28</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyra, the same,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 4, 1, 16</span></i>
			: arcus, i. e. <i>the constellation
				Sagittarius</i> (because orig. the Thessalian
			centaur Chiron), <i><span class="en">id. M. 2, 81</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Haemŏ-nĭdes</span></b> , ae,
				m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἱμονίδης</span>,
				<i>a Hœmonian</i> or <i>Thessalian;</i> in plur., i. q. Argonautae,
				<i>the Argonauts</i>, <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 4,
				506</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hae-mŏnis</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aem-</span></b> ),
				ĭdis, f., <i>a
				Thessalian woman</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 13, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Luc. 6,
			436</span></i>; <i><span class="en">590</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
